      "valueMarkdown": "Preventive Care and Wellness (Patient-level linear) test case. Olga (66) has a mammogram within 27 months and pneumococcal vaccination, but her most recent colonoscopy is more than 10 years old. Her blood pressure was not obtained for a medical reason at her first visit (a denominator exception) but was normal at her preventive visit. She has a limited life expectancy, which is a denominator exception for tobacco screening. Component status: BCS: met; HBP: met; CCS: not met; PVS: met; TSC group 1: exception; TSC group 2: n/a. Expected measure observation 3 / 4 = 0.75."
